Freeciv @VERSION@ for AmigaOS 3.x (AmiCradle)
=====================================================

Freeciv is the open-source empire-building strategy game in the manner of
Civilization: found cities, research, trade, make war and peace, from
4000 BC to the space age. This is its AmigaOS 3.x build for a 68040 or
68060 with an FPU: the SDL 2 client (through GFOpenGPU) and the server,
English only. Status: TESTING, not a release.

Requirements
------------

- AmigaOS 3.2, a 68040 or 68060 with an FPU, AmiCradle or an RTG board,
  and plenty of fast RAM (the client alone used about 45 MB).
- GFOpenGPU's SDL2.module and SDL2_image.module in LIBS:GFOpenGPU/.
- bsdsocket.library (GFOpenSocket): the client talks to its own server
  on this machine.

Installing
----------

Unpack the archive where you keep games (lha x freeciv-...lha Games:) and
open the Freeciv drawer. Settings and saves go to the drawer's User
drawer.

Playing
-------

- Double-click Freeciv: IconX runs the Freeciv script, which gives the
  client a large stack and starts it. "Start New Game" starts the server
  beside it.
- From a Shell: cd to the drawer, then Execute Freeciv.
- Shift+Return ends a turn. Options, Save Game and Load Game are in the
  client's menu; Options, Quit closes the client and the server with it.

Licence
-------

Freeciv and its data are GPL-2.0-or-later (COPYING); the source is at
https://github.com/freeciv/freeciv. The icons are drawn from Freeciv's own
client icon.

